  "cause": "Matcher.Add retains each differing non-nullable counter even once both satisfy the minimum. Repeated content partitions grow without useful language distinction; Q005 (e1+){1,1000} on 1000 e1 children forces at least C(1000,3)=166167000 charged pair inspections in one state family. This is a static lower bound, not timing or runtime measurement.",
  "proposed_boundary": "Same PC/flags and componentwise smaller repetition counters after both meet minimum can represent a superset of future continuations. Prove this using independent finite-language enumeration; retain differing below-minimum states and actual finite maxima. Use existing charges/polls, no cap increase or clamp shortcut.",
